    <briefdescription>
<para>Type-erased interface for service-staff management operations. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Exposes three domain operations — add, remove and invite — each in a synchronous callback form and a coroutine (<computeroutput>drogon::Task&lt;void&gt;</computeroutput>) form. The staff route registry holds concrete controllers behind this base and dispatches to them via a <computeroutput>std::variant</computeroutput> over the service entity type.</para>
<para>In plain words: &quot;synchronous&quot; means the caller gets the answer through a callback function, while the coroutine (<computeroutput>drogon::Task&lt;void&gt;</computeroutput>) versions can be paused with co_await so the server can do other work meanwhile. &quot;Virtual dispatch&quot; means a call made through this base automatically runs the real object&apos;s version. A <computeroutput>std::variant</computeroutput> is like a box that can hold one of several different controller types at a time.</para>
<para>Invocation contract shared by every method:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>callback</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>std::function&lt;void(int, const std::string&amp;)&gt;</computeroutput>, it is moved through the call chain and, by contract, invoked once on each completion path, including failures. Its first argument is an <ref refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2_1_1Http_1a6199aeb84d745378b1befef28d78892f" kindref="member">api::v2::Http::Status</ref> code, the second a response body.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>requester</computeroutput> is the authenticated caller; implementations require permission to manage staff of the target service before performing any side effect.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>data</computeroutput> is a non-owning view of the raw JSON request body, valid only for the call; it must carry the target service id (<computeroutput>id</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>nominee_id</computeroutput>) used for authorisation.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The <computeroutput>*Async</computeroutput> methods must be co_awaited; the HTTP layer wraps them in <computeroutput>drogon::async_run</computeroutput> and builds the reply from the callback result. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The interface itself is stateless; behaviour lives in <ref refid="classStaffController" kindref="compound">StaffController</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classStaffController" kindref="compound">StaffController</ref>, <ref refid="classController" kindref="compound">Controller</ref>, <ref refid="controller_8hpp_1aa21c1eb0e46bd1813cc4cba55771c0a3" kindref="member">GateKeeper</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
